WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:08.827
<v Audio Description>Visual scene one: Card one glows amber beside a spinning cyan crystal core wrapped in clear glass, linked by spokes to six outer gate pads.

2
00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:16.115
<v Presenter>First, you write a program once as one clear blueprint, and the computer generates matching code across languages.

3
00:00:16.455 --> 00:00:26.657
<v Audio Description>Visual scene two: Card two shines cyan. Five outer spokes glow emerald for valid inputs, while the sixth spoke glows rose to stop an invalid input safely.

4
00:00:26.997 --> 00:00:34.587
<v Presenter>Second, every possible input must have a declared outcome up front, preventing hidden crashes before anything runs.

5
00:00:34.927 --> 00:00:43.765
<v Audio Description>Visual scene three: Card three lights up emerald beneath the emerald orbit ring, showing two thousand two hundred twenty-one passing checks with zero failures.

6
00:00:44.105 --> 00:00:50.263
<v Presenter>Third, every repair that passes the checker is saved and reused, so you never pay twice for one fix.
